extends RefCounted

const TOPICS := [
	["Deployment", "Select a sector and difficulty at Deploy. Act I ends at the miniboss, then the Act II gate opens. Defeat the guardian in Act II, open the boss cache and reach the extraction pad to bank the rewards.", "Clear a sector on Normal to unlock Hard there and improve your odds of rare loot. Clear every sector on Hard to unlock Expert. In co-op, every operator needs the difficulty unlocked. The NOVA Archive shows a sector's loot after your first clear."],
	["Movement & traversal", "Jump and dash across gaps. Hold toward a wall while airborne to slide down it, then jump to climb. Press up as you reach ladders or vines to grab them. On a drop-through deck, hold crouch and press the drop command.", "The ground dash becomes a slide and stays low while overhead geometry blocks standing. Check Keyboard & Mouse or Controller in Settings for your exact bindings."],
	["Buster, saber & suits", "Tap fire for one Buster shot. Hold it to charge and release. A charged standard shot gets through a raised purple shield. Regular shots can hit from behind or while the guard is down. Tap melee in rhythm for the saber combo, or hold and release for a ranged slice.", "Defeating a guardian unlocks its suit for the current run. Cycle suits with the shoulder buttons or the bound swap controls. Boss weapons use energy, so switch back to the standard frame when your reserve is low."],
	["Checkpoints & reconstruction", "Touch a checkpoint to set your return point. A death uses a life. Run out of lives and NOVA reconstructs you at the station. You can deploy to any previously unlocked sector.", "Reconstruction resets your Operator Level and run suits and clears your equipped gear and quick slots. Your Player Level, stored items, banked currency, learned recipes and permanent enhancements carry over."],
	["Shop & currency", "Spend Bolts at the Shop on recovery supplies, buffs and crafting materials. Better stock unlocks at Player Level 5 and every five levels after that. Purchases go into your carried inventory. Visit Equipment and use the Storage tab to deposit them.", "Boss clears and challenges reward Core Shards. Spend them on permanent talents in Core Ascension, in the Workshop."],
	["Core Ascension", "Spend Core Shards in Survivability, Damage or Scavenger. Install one talent in each earlier tier to advance in that branch. Every talent has three ranks. Tier 5 introduces a capstone at Player Level 28 that can reach Rank III at Player Level 50.", "Field Reboot lets you revive one downed ally per boss attempt. Get close to the ally marker and press Field Interact, then stay close and avoid damage until the reboot finishes. Higher ranks restore more HP."],
	["Foundry replay", "The Kiln Warden awards a choice of one run module. In Act II, the low cooling tunnel leads to recovery supplies. The upper furnace gantry leads to a weapon cache.", "Hit the cooling deck coupler with Magma Breaker or a charged saber wave to raise a bridge. On Expert, shoot the lit relief valve after the Forge Titan's rupture charge to vent the flames and expose his core."],
	["Blueprint hunts", "After your first clear, visit the NOVA Archive and pin a blueprint from that sector's boss cache. Deploy shows the source, minimum difficulty, required Operator Level and progress.", "Three eligible extractions earn the pinned blueprint if it hasn't dropped. Your hunt progress stays with the operator when saved."],
	["Equipment & Storage", "In Gear, choose a socket to see compatible items. Equip one item per socket and check the operator's stats. Use Storage to browse or transfer gear, supplies, blueprints and materials.", "Salvage recovered in a mission goes to Storage when you extract. Shop purchases stay in your carried inventory until you move them. Equipped gear stays at risk on a run."],
	["Quick slots", "Assign a supply to a D-pad direction from Equipment or the mission pause inventory. Each direction holds one item type, up to three of that item. The upper limit for an inventory stack is 100.", "Press a direction during gameplay to use one supply. Health and energy supplies only consume when there is something to restore. Recovery items and temporary buffs are described on their item cards."],
	["Blueprints & Crafting", "Select a blueprint in Storage and confirm Learn Blueprint. Learning consumes the item and unlocks its recipe in Workshop. Review the material cost and level requirement before fabricating.", "Move an unused blueprint into the Blueprint Pouch to share it in the station with a co-op teammate. The pouch has eight slots. Boss caches guarantee a blueprint and can also contain materials and supplies."],
	["Social & co-op", "Use Social to add friends, send whispers and accept invites. Start a Group from Deploy. The party leader selects the sector and starts the mission. Each operator has an independent camera.", "Loot and inventory are personal. The party shares kill XP and boss suit unlocks. All operators must reach the boss door and cross it before the fight starts."],
	["Challenges", "Each unlocked sector has five challenges. Requirements can include reaching Act II, extracting at high health, moving quickly or gathering salvage.", "Finish the set to start the 24-hour reset timer. The clock keeps counting when the game is closed. The challenge panel shows rewards and the time until a new set arrives."],
	["System & Save", "Use the System pad to save your operator manually. Operator slots are managed from the title screen. A save includes banked progress and the current deployment when available.", "Settings covers audio, video, gameplay, keyboard and controller bindings, and installed game updates. Toggle first-time hub tips in Gameplay. This manual remains available either way."],
]
